<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Osaka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1614">1614</a>–<a href="/years/1615">1615</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka">Osaka</a> was a series of campaigns in 1614–1615 in which the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka-castle">Osaka Castle</a>, held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-clan">Toyotomi</a> family. The castle fell and the Toyotomi line was destroyed. This removed the last rival source of legitimacy and completed Tokugawa control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-osaka.jpg" alt="Siege of Osaka" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utagawa Yoshitora · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osakarakuzyou_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
